1
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:02,767
Cough! Cough!

2
00:00:02,767 --> 00:00:04,283
Is everyone okay?

3
00:00:04,283 --> 00:00:05,623
I'm fine

4
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:06,566
Smile?

5
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:07,450
Multiple abrasions

6
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:08,950
But no impairment to function

7
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:10,650
Thank goodness

8
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:11,767
Smile's so tiny, yet

9
00:00:11,782 --> 00:00:13,767
she's weirdly tough

10
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:15,733
Still though…

11
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,550
What exactly is going on here?

12
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:21,283
The output of that last attack was…

13
00:00:21,283 --> 00:00:23,516
compared to when we stopped the true Aldebaran's descent,

14
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,117
over 120%

15
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:27,183
We should have definitely defeated it…

16
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:28,183


17
00:00:29,633 --> 00:00:31,100
Smile!

18
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:35,850
Wh— what do we do?

19
00:00:36,483 --> 00:00:38,583
The blood… it won't stop!

20
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:43,433
…A bonfire will one day be extinguished,

21
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:45,817
and even the greatest of stars

22
00:00:45,867 --> 00:00:48,500
will crumble to dust in time

23
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:52,366
Such is the law of all things, the providence of the cosmos

24
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:58,250
You fleeting sparks, born for but a moment in the witch's wheel—

25
00:00:59,067 --> 00:01:01,817
why do you defy providence?

26
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:03,600
That's…

27
00:01:03,917 --> 00:01:05,400
not Aldebaran

28
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,367
Someone merely descended before us

29
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:11,667
using Aldebaran's body as a vessel…

30
00:01:12,217 --> 00:01:14,234
That's definitely… what I saw in my dreams…

31
00:01:15,067 --> 00:01:17,450
I am the one who conceives the void…

32
00:01:18,450 --> 00:01:19,983
[Laniakea]

33
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,783
To extinguish the forbidden sparks you carry,

34
00:01:24,317 --> 00:01:29,434
I have come forth from eternal nothingness and silence

35
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,533
Matter… space… everything is being broken down…

36
00:01:39,967 --> 00:01:42,467
At this rate, all of Lavistar will be destroyed!

37
00:01:43,283 --> 00:01:44,883
Luna! Is there anything we can do?!

38
00:01:46,533 --> 00:01:47,800


39
00:01:47,950 --> 00:01:49,067
So in the end…

40
00:01:49,383 --> 00:01:51,616
it comes to this

41
00:01:51,733 --> 00:01:52,583
Luna…?

42
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:59,767
I… actually knew

43
00:02:00,183 --> 00:02:02,683
that there was never any hope for this mission

44
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,283
I am an Oracle, after all

45
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:09,800
The greatest one in all of Lavistar, at that

46
00:02:11,217 --> 00:02:13,350
I knew the Hall of Stars would be emptied,

47
00:02:13,483 --> 00:02:15,916
and that we would fail— all of it

48
00:02:17,017 --> 00:02:19,134
Over and over… over and over…

49
00:02:19,767 --> 00:02:22,501
I've seen this play out in my dreams more times than I can count

50
00:02:22,950 --> 00:02:24,717
No matter what choice we make

51
00:02:25,167 --> 00:02:27,900
Because I already know the ending won't change…

52
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:31,150
I gave up on clinging to hope long ago

53
00:02:31,150 --> 00:02:32,433
That's all

54
00:02:32,783 --> 00:02:33,800
Don't give up!

55
00:02:33,950 --> 00:02:35,650
I know the future can still change!

56
00:02:35,833 --> 00:02:37,983
No, it can't

57
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:40,733
Because…

58
00:02:42,583 --> 00:02:45,250
There was never a future that could be changed

59
00:02:45,467 --> 00:02:48,034
This is where everything ends

60
00:02:51,283 --> 00:02:52,550
Actually, I…

61
00:02:52,717 --> 00:02:54,900
There's something I never told you all

62
00:02:55,733 --> 00:02:57,433
The reason I took on this mission…

63
00:02:58,217 --> 00:02:59,433
The reason I came here…

64
00:03:00,183 --> 00:03:01,283
I know

65
00:03:01,883 --> 00:03:03,416
It was to find [that person], wasn't it?

66
00:03:04,683 --> 00:03:06,000


67
00:03:06,367 --> 00:03:07,167
You too…

68
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:09,333
You remember that person?

69
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:14,667
I always wondered

70
00:03:14,717 --> 00:03:16,600
The [Hall of Stars] should have

71
00:03:16,617 --> 00:03:18,734
faded away long ago…

72
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:22,117
The Stella Archive we gained through the [Journey]…

73
00:03:22,583 --> 00:03:26,383
The power left behind by the [Star Savior]… who granted it to us?

74
00:03:27,033 --> 00:03:29,616
Every time I thought about it, someone would cross my mind

75
00:03:31,433 --> 00:03:33,250
I can't remember their face

76
00:03:34,483 --> 00:03:36,916
And their voice is faint…

77
00:03:38,767 --> 00:03:41,867
But surely, someone who was right there beside us

78
00:03:43,167 --> 00:03:44,717
So go

79
00:03:45,267 --> 00:03:47,000
Go and find that person

80
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,733
The path… I'll open it for you

81
00:03:52,567 --> 00:03:55,584
I am the bearer of the Moon Staff, after all!

82
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,040
The power of the Stella Archive within me—

83
00:03:59,050 --> 00:04:00,483
If I use it all…

84
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,833
I'm sure I can open a path
to [that person]

85
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:04,150
I can do it

86
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:07,333
But…

87
00:04:08,017 --> 00:04:09,267
After I'm gone

88
00:04:10,383 --> 00:04:12,200
What about you and Smile…

89
00:04:13,550 --> 00:04:14,617
…Did someone call for me?

90
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,100
Smile! Are you okay?
- Smile!

91
00:04:17,133 --> 00:04:18,766
Cough…

92
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:21,350
My fluid loss rate is a bit high…

93
00:04:21,467 --> 00:04:23,950
But compared to being worked to the bone

94
00:04:23,950 --> 00:04:25,483
by that tyrant Captain Asherah all this time

95
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:27,950
This is nothing

96
00:04:28,683 --> 00:04:29,500
And…

97
00:04:30,383 --> 00:04:32,866
I heard everything while I was lying there

98
00:04:33,417 --> 00:04:36,167
I'm pretty sure I remember [that person] too

99
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:38,933
They were the one who… mended the loose stitching

100
00:04:38,933 --> 00:04:41,200
on my cat squad

101
00:04:42,267 --> 00:04:43,783
So…

102
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:46,967
Stop crying and smile, Asherah.

103
00:04:47,317 --> 00:04:48,484
Smile…

104
00:04:49,467 --> 00:04:51,050
My sister told me—

105
00:04:51,517 --> 00:04:53,200
when you're happy, you should smile.

106
00:04:53,783 --> 00:04:56,083
But when you're sad and hurting…

107
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:58,633
you should smile even bigger.

108
00:04:59,083 --> 00:05:02,333
I'm sure [that person] loves smiles too.

109
00:05:03,367 --> 00:05:05,917
I'll… show you how.

110
00:05:06,650 --> 00:05:09,667
Like this… say cheese!

111
00:05:12,033 --> 00:05:13,550
…Yeah.

112
00:05:13,667 --> 00:05:14,984
I'll smile.

113
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,483
No matter how hard things get,

114
00:05:17,983 --> 00:05:20,416
I'll definitely come back.

115
00:05:20,533 --> 00:05:22,350
Together with [that person]!

116
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,834
Alright! Ready?

117
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:34,017
I'm gonna burn through every last bit of the Stella Archive's power

118
00:05:34,117 --> 00:05:35,767
and open the portal through time and space!

119
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:41,000
Three!

120
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:43,500
Two!

121
00:05:44,067 --> 00:05:45,200
One!

122
00:05:45,650 --> 00:05:46,800
Open!

123
00:06:04,850 --> 00:06:07,067
Hey… Luna…

124
00:06:07,567 --> 00:06:10,650
How was my smile…?

125
00:06:11,483 --> 00:06:14,133
Do you think… I could show my sister…

126
00:06:14,367 --> 00:06:17,017
with my head held high…?

127
00:06:17,550 --> 00:06:19,333
…It was totally awkward.

128
00:06:20,283 --> 00:06:21,450
But…

129
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,550
it was really beautiful.

130
00:06:23,950 --> 00:06:25,400
Heh…

131
00:06:26,217 --> 00:06:29,117
I'm glad…

132
00:06:35,083 --> 00:06:36,583
Smile…?

133
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:41,567


134
00:06:42,933 --> 00:06:46,116
You did great, Smile.

135
00:06:46,650 --> 00:06:48,783
So for now,

136
00:06:48,833 --> 00:06:51,050
it's okay to rest.

137
00:06:52,267 --> 00:06:55,167
Even if this is truly the end…

138
00:06:55,250 --> 00:06:58,500
even if every possibility has been closed off…

139
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:01,317
I know [that person] will come

140
00:07:01,783 --> 00:07:05,333
and open the way forward.

